I think the problem as stated is insufficiently general. After all,
why doesn't it apply with equal force to "I need eight maids a-milking?"
Does that mean some specific eight maids, or any eight maids?
In other contexts we talk about le bi vs. bi lo.

Any eight would be {mi nitcu lo'e nixli bimei},
"I need Mr Maid Eightsome" or we could also say {mi biroi
nitcu lo'e nixli}, "I need Mr Maid eight times".

{mi nitcu bi lo nixli} means that there are eight and only eight
maids such that I need each of them.

mu'o mi'e xorxes











